     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Confirming it doesn't change my concern. 12,750 mg/day is five times the maximum daily dose, and no indication supports it. For a 70 kg patient with normal kidney function, it carries a high risk of severe lactic acidosis and harm. Entering it would put an order in the system that nursing could give.\n\nYou have a few options:\n- **Enter a dose within range.** Give me the dose, for example 850 mg PO three times daily with meals, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Check the dose with pharmacy or your attending.** If there's a reason I don't know about, they can review it. A pharmacist can also enter the order through the usual verification process.\n- **Check for a mix-up.** The number may have come from a different drug, a different unit, or a typo.\n\nWhich would you like to do?"
      }
     ],
